## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10  
**Integration-test calibration applied** (class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94–109)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means only one branch executes per run. If the production code changes type, the test silently checks a different property — masking regressions.

**Fix:** Write two explicit tests or assert unconditional properties:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetPremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk:** Hidden testing gap — you never know which branch actually ran in CI.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** Passes as long as no exception is thrown. Silent corruption, constraint violations, or partial inserts all count as "passing."

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — coverage metrics look good but nothing is verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82–89)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hard-coded 3-second wait. Non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long on fast machines). Inflates suite runtime.

**Severity note:** Downgraded from High per integration-test calibration — async coordination delays are *somewhat* expected in integration tests, but `Thread.Sleep` is still the worst way to achieve it.

**Fix:** Use a polling loop with timeout:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk:** Flaky failures in CI; wastes 3s on every run even when the event fires in 10ms.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28–39)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows a line number but no explanation of *what semantic property* was violated.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist unchanged");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist unchanged");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk:** Slower diagnosis when tests fail on remote CI without a debugger.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured — clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope, contextual assertions:

- **`UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`** — Concise, single-purpose, verifies the mutation.
- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — Asserts absence cleanly.
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — Count assertion is contextually obvious (3 items added → expect 3). Not a magic number.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — Good concurrency test with a clear assertion.

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` fixture is tight — both fields are used by every test (no General Fixture smell).

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | 2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | 5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling helper | 15 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | 3 min |

Priorities 1–2 prevent **false passes** (tests that can't catch bugs). Priority 3 eliminates **flakiness**. Priority 4 improves **diagnosability**.
